R(25,'AIR 2005 SC 4391','Controller of Defence Accounts (Pension) and others v. S. Balachandran Nair','AIR 2005 SC 4391','follows','court_own','In the case of Controller of Defence Accounts (Pension) and others v. S. Balachandran Nair reported in AIR 2005 SC 4391 and the decision in Union of India and another v. Baljit Singh reported in 1996 (11) SCC 315 held that Medical Board\'s opinion to the effect that illness. and disability suffered by the respondent therein was not attributable to military service cannot be substituted by the court','high','Court states holding and then applies "aforesaid legal position" to the facts (para 11).')
