R(27,"Ram Avtar's case (supra)","Ram Avtar",RA,'follows','court_own',"Learned counsel for the petitioners has not been able to dispute the said proposition of law having been settled by the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India in Ram Avtar's case (supra) to the effect that percentage of disability to be rounded off of the disability element from 30% to 50% in the present case.",'high','Citation 2014 SCC Online SC 1761 from p.3.')
R(27,'Civil Appeal No.11311 of 2025','Union of India and others vs. Reet MP Singh and another',RM,'follows','court_own',"Further, in a recent judgment in Civil Appeal No.11311 of 2025 titled as Union of India and others vs. Reet MP Singh and another, decided on 01.09.2025, the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India by placing reliance upon Ram Avtar's case (supra), has again reiterated that the benefit of rounding off the disability element, cannot be denied.",'high','Court relies on it (para 10).')
