E86a="Learned counsel for the petitioners has not been able to dispute the said proposition of law having been settled by the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India in Dharamvir Singh's case (supra) & Ram Avtar's case (supra) to the effect that percentage of disability is to be rounded off"
E86b="Further, in a recent judgment in Civil Appeal No.11311 of 2025 titled as Union of India and others vs. Reet MP Singh and another, decided on 01.09.2025, the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India by placing reliance upon Ram Avtar's case (supra) as well as Bijender Singh vs. Union of India and others, 2025 SCC Online SC 895, has again reiterated that the benefit of rounding off the disability element so as to grant the disability pension cannot be denied."
E86c="Keeping in view the facts and circumstance of the present case as well as the settled principle of law settled in Dharamvir Singh's case (supra), Ram Avtar's case (supra) as well as Reet MP Singh case (supra), once at the time of enrolment, respondent No.1 was medically examined and was found to be fit"
